  "id": "COMPOUND:18648 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Nigrolineaxanthone F is implicated in targeting Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is a key enzyme involved in the metabolism of various compounds. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol, all of which are known to interact with HepG2 cells. The evidence suggests that Nigrolineaxanthone F may exert its biological effects through a shared mechanism of action, targeting a common downstream component that ultimately leads to cellular effects on HepG2. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Nigrolineaxanthone F in modulating cellular processes through the SDR family, with the final effect observed in HepG2 cells. The evidence supports a mechanism where Nigrolineaxanthone F may act as a modulator of the SDR family, influencing cellular responses that culminate in the observed effects on HepG2.",
